<title>MEXICO: Salina Cruz port shut; Pemex shipping not affected.</title>
<headline>Salina Cruz port shut; Pemex shipping not affected.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The closure of the Salina Cruz port in Oaxaca state did not halt shipping crude oil shipping activity, terminal sources said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Luis Contreras of the Salina Cruz terminal said Petroleos Mexicanos shipping was not affected by strong winds that closed the port to smaller boats from 800 local time Tuesday to 1000 local time Wednesday.</p>
<p>Salina Cruz exported an daily average 90,000 barrels of oil to Japan during the first half of the year, a Pemex spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7903</p>
